只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH (DeepSeek Harness) browser plugin: your agent drives the Chrome you already use. Native messaging + real CDP, no port, no Connect button, 12 browser_* tools, on the Chrome Web Store. · 让 DSH 在你正在用的 Chrome 里动手。","id":"gh:1408188488","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-chrome-bridge","slug":"OrderG-X/dsh-chrome-bridge","topics":["ai-agent","automation","browser","browser-automation","browser-extension","browser-use","cdp","chrome","chrome-devtools-protocol","chrome-extension","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","linux","macos","native-messaging","plugin","web-automation","windows"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH (DeepSeek Harness) browser plugin: your agent drives the Chrome you already use. Native messagin"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"g + real CDP, no port, no Connect button, 12 browser_* tools, on the Chrome Web Store. · 让 DSH 在你正在用"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" no port, no Connect button, 12 browser_* tools, on the Chrome Web Store. · 让 DSH 在你正在用的 Chrome 里动手。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"= 116\" />"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"= 18\" />"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English ·\n简体中文 ·\nDevelopment notes"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Give your DSH agent hands inside the Chrome you are already using** — your logins, your tabs, your"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" session. Install once, no Connect button, ever."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> **What it is:** a DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin that lets the model operate the Chrome you already"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" use: open pages, click, type, fill in forms, read pages, take screenshots and work across tabs, wit"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"h your existing logins.\n>\n> **Use it for:** \"fill in this web form\", \"check this admin page for me\","},{"id":"p6s4","text":" \"screenshot this site\", or anything else the model has to do inside a browser.\n>\n> **Install:** on "},{"id":"p6s5","text":"the DSH Plugins page, click Add plugin and enter `dsh-chrome-bridge` (an npm package), restart DSH, "},{"id":"p6s6","text":"then add the DSH Bridge extension from the Chrome Web Store. Needs macOS, Windows or Linux, Chrome 1"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"16+ and Node.js 18+."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Every click flies a cursor to the target and labels what it is doing. It renders *inside the page*, "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"so it lands in screenshots too — you and the model look at the same picture."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## ✨ Why another browser bridge?"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Every existing option makes you click something, every time:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Option | What goes wrong |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| `chrome-devtools-mcp --autoConnect` | Chrome asks *\"Allow remote debugging?\"* on **every** connect"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ion |\n| Browser MCP (store extension) | You must click the extension icon → **Connect** on **every**"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" tab |\n| WebSocket-based bridges | Open a TCP port and trust anything that can reach it |\n| **dsh-ch"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"rome-bridge** | Nothing to click. Nothing listening on a port. |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Three things make the difference:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- 🔌 **Native messaging, not a port.** The extension talks to a local Node host over Chrome's native "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"messaging pipe; the CLI reaches the host through a `0600` Unix socket guarded by a token. No TCP por"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"t to scan, no origin to spoof.\n- 🎯 **`chrome.debugger`, not injected scripts.** Clicks and keystroke"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"s are dispatched as real CDP `Input.*` events, so they carry a user gesture — popups open, focus wor"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"ks, and sites that reject synthetic events behave normally. Screenshots, network, console and raw CD"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"P come for free.\n- 👀 **A cursor the human can see.** A translucent light-blue arrow with a \"🌐 DSH\" n"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"ame tag glides along a gentle arc to the target; the tag says what it is doing (click / type / drag "},{"id":"p13s8","text":"/ scroll) and each click leaves a soft ripple. It shares one style with the desktop cursor of dsh-ma"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"c-computer-use (solid there, with a monitor icon), so you can tell at a glance whether the work is i"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"n the browser or on the desktop. It sits above modals and fullscreen, and picks up where it was afte"},{"id":"p13s11","text":"r a navigation. Because it is rendered inside the page, **it appears in screenshots**."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## 🏗 Architecture"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"**This repo ships no agent** — the agent above is DSH's own; we only give it hands."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The extension ID is fixed by the public key embedded in `plugin/vendor/extension/manifest.json`, so "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"it is **identical on every machine** and the native-host registration never needs editing. The Web S"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"tore build has its own store-assigned ID; the host accepts both."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## 🚀 Install"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**The host ships inside the plugin package.** Adding the plugin copies the native host and the MV3 e"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"xtension into place and registers native messaging for you — no `git clone`, no `install.sh`, no `py"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"n into place and registers native messaging for you — no `git clone`, no `install.sh`, no `python3`."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Requirements: **macOS, Windows or Linux**, **Google Chrome 116+**, **Node.js 18+**."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### 👀 What you see while it works"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"- **Click the toolbar icon** for a live panel: whether Chrome ↔ local host ↔ DSH are connected, **wh"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ich DSH sessions are driving which tabs** (jump to a tab, or release it with one click), the last ac"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"tions with their errors, a **pause switch** that makes the browser off-limits until you turn it back"},{"id":"p23s4","text":" on, and *copy diagnostics* for bug reports. The icon badge shows how many tabs are under control (`"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"!` = host down, `⏸` = paused).\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## 🔒 Security"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Be honest about what this is: **the extension can read and control every page you are logged into.**"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- The bridge is **local-only**. Native messaging is a private pipe; the CLI socket is `0600` and add"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"itionally token-guarded. **It opens no network listener of its own** (the DSH settings card goes thr"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"ough DSH's built-in local web server; that route only accepts loopback, rejects cross-site requests,"},{"id":"p26s4","text":" and cannot resume control).\n- Chrome shows a permanent *\"… is debugging this browser\"* banner while"},{"id":"p26s5","text":" attached. That banner is the point — you can always see that it is active.\n- Anything that can alre"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"ady run as your user can read your Chrome profile; this does not widen that boundary. It does make i"},{"id":"p26s7","text":"t *convenient*, which is worth a thought before leaving an agent unattended.\n- **Once the DSH plugin"},{"id":"p26s8","text":" is installed, the model drives your browser without asking.** Plugin tools run inside the DSH host "},{"id":"p26s9","text":"process, so they are *not* gated by the workspace sandbox or the approval prompts that guard `bash`."},{"id":"p26s10","text":" That is what \"native\" buys you — and it means an unattended agent holds your browser. Disable the p"},{"id":"p26s11","text":"lugin in the sidebar if you want that gate back.\n- Detach any time: click **Cancel** on the banner, "},{"id":"p26s12","text":"or `cb detach <tab>`."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## ⚠️ Limitations"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **Windows and Linux support is new** — a daily CI run on GitHub's Windows and Linux machines insta"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"lls it, connects a real Chrome and reads a page, but it has not been used on a real person's PC yet."},{"id":"p28s3","text":" Please open an issue if something breaks. On Windows it also registers for Edge (untested).\n- **`ch"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"rome://` pages are unreachable** — Chrome forbids injection there. Use a normal tab.\n- An `alert()` "},{"id":"p28s5","text":"blocks the page: `cb info` warns you, `cb dialog accept` releases it.\n- Chrome defers `alert()` in b"},{"id":"p28s6","text":"ackground tabs until the tab is focused.\n- Without the Web Store, Chrome 137+ (no more `--load-exten"},{"id":"p28s7","text":"sion`) needs one manual load through `chrome://extensions`.\n- The Web Store build lags the repo a li"},{"id":"p28s8","text":"ttle: new extension versions wait for store review."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
